i2c: pxa — build the CE5300 I2C on x86_64 (not just X86_32)

openHC runs a 64-bit kernel (CEFDK's bootlinux starts a bzImage in long mode),
but drivers/i2c/busses/Kconfig gates both the driver and its PCI glue on X86_32:

    I2C_PXA      depends on ... || (X86_32 && PCI && OF) || ...
    I2C_PXA_PCI  def_bool I2C_PXA && X86_32 && PCI && OF

So on x86_64 CONFIG_I2C_PXA=y is dropped in silence — the symbol's dependency is
unmet, exactly the "assignment to an unavailable symbol vanishes" trap — and
i2c-pxa-pci is never compiled. The result is NO i2c bus at all: the CE5300's
four I2C controllers (PCI 8086:2e68) never enumerate, and that takes with it the
LM75 heatsink sensor (so ohc-fand finds no hwmon and exits, leaving the fan
stopped and uncontrolled), the DS1339 RTC, and the ADAU1451 audio codec. On the
live EA1 this showed as an empty /sys/bus/i2c and no /sys/class/hwmon.

The X86_32 restriction is historical: the only in-tree user was the 32-bit
CE4100/Sodaville. The CE5300 is the same I2C block reached over the same PCI
function, and patch 0001 already makes i2c-pxa-pci enumerate WITHOUT a device
tree (it hands each BAR to a platform device when of_node is NULL), so the OF
dependency is not needed either. Widen both to X86 and drop OF.

Scope: EA family only (board/ea-common/patches), the only openHC target on this
SoC. Pairs with 0001 (enumerate without DT).

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/Kconfig
@@ -1029,14 +1029,14 @@
 
 config I2C_PXA
 	tristate "Intel PXA2XX I2C adapter"
-	depends on ARCH_PXA || ARCH_MMP || ARCH_MVEBU || (X86_32 && PCI && OF) || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARCH_PXA || ARCH_MMP || ARCH_MVEBU || (X86 && PCI) || COMPILE_TEST
 	help
 	  If you have devices in the PXA I2C bus, say yes to this option.
 	  This driver can also be built as a module.  If so, the module
 	  will be called i2c-pxa.
 
 config I2C_PXA_PCI
-	def_bool I2C_PXA && X86_32 && PCI && OF
+	def_bool I2C_PXA && X86 && PCI
 
 config I2C_PXA_SLAVE
 	bool "Intel PXA2XX I2C Slave comms support"
